From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 07:25:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: keep a received WhatsApp sticker as WebP

A sticker received on WhatsApp could not be sent back as a sticker.
The plugin turned it into a PNG on download, because the old WebKit
could not draw WebP, and the Messaging app offers only a .webp as a
sticker; a PNG would go out as a picture. It also kept only the first
frame of an animated sticker.

Keep the sticker as it came, as <hash>.webp with image/webp: WAM's
Chromium draws WebP, animated too. It is now streamed into its file
like other WhatsApp media rather than fetched into memory, which was
only needed for the transcoding. A Lottie sticker, which is no WebP,
keeps the type it came with.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
